;; sarutahiko-factory-r0 — 施工ロボット登録台帳 (construction-robot registry),
;; Datomic-style EDN. SSoT for which robot performs each construction step.
;; Same shape + toolchain as giemon-factory-r0/robots.edn (ADR-2606010030).
;;
;; NOTE — two robot LAYERS exist in this plant, do not conflate them:
;;   (1) CONSTRUCTION robots (this file) — the tatekata 建方 fleet that BUILDS the
;;       plant (ADR-2605250715). construction.edn :step/robot references these.
;;   (2) PRODUCTION robots — the truck-line robots that, once built, MANUFACTURE
;;       trucks: arm6 cells (frame-weld/spot-weld/paint/harness/inspect),
;;       part-AGVs, and the F10 積込ロボット loader. Those live in
;;       factory.scene.json (cells / agvs / loaders) and building.edn group F,
;;       and are simulated by the kami-app crate, NOT here.
;;
;; :robot/reach-m   manipulator reach (m) — used by the buildability check
;; :robot/base      [length width] of the robot footprint (m)
;; :robot/cycle-min nominal cycle time per unit of work (minutes)
;; :robot/mobile    true = self-relocating base (covers a zone), false = fixed
;; :robot/process   material process it drives: deposition | thermal-weld | none
;; :robot/maturity  HONEST real-world maturity of this robot class today:
;;                  field-trial | partial | human-collab  (none is "fully autonomous")

{:robot/meta
 {:robot/of    "sarutahiko-factory-r0"
  :robot/note  "R0 design assignment for BUILDING the truck plant (tatekata 建方 fleet). Maturity is the HONEST state of each robot class in real construction today — NONE is a turnkey autonomous solution. The truck-line production robots (incl. 積込ロボット) are NOT in this file; they are in factory.scene.json + building.edn group F."}

